 finally revealed a huge secret about  those boxy apple watch renders that he  kept hidden from all of us the entire  time and this is probably the biggest  piece of evidence for my second theory  actually being true and it would  essentially mean that we're finally  going to be getting the flat sided  redesign with the apple watch series 8  pro model and if you're wondering what i  mean by pro model i'll explain after i  get into john's secret mac rumors  recently created a new podcast where  they invited john prosser to join as a  guest and of course they hammered him on  the whole boxy design leak that never  came to light and within this podcast he  ended up revealing exactly what went  wrong apparently he actually received a  real image of a prototype flat sided  apple watch design in the new starlight  finish which is a huge piece of evidence  for these leaks not being faked by apple  and john even confirmed that after the  september event none of his sources  within apple were caught so this means  that apple didn't fabricate all this  stuff to intentionally weed out the  sources and it means that these design  leaks are actually true but going even  further he ended up revealing the  original renders from his sources that  he kept a secret from the very beginning  and to my shock those renders showed not  one but two apple watch designs and  according to john he initially thought  that the smaller watch on the left was  simply the regular series 6 that we  already had at the time with the new  boxy one on the right side which was  supposed to be the new boxy series 7  design but nope he was wrong after apple  revealed the more rounded true series 7  he looked back at the renders and  realized that the watch on the left was  actually a more rounded series 7 design  which ended up getting released and is  likely the intended design for the  regular series 8 model as well and then  the larger one on the right was most  likely meant to be a brand new extra  series 8 model which i personally  believe is the new rugged or explorer  edition which ended up getting delayed  until 2022 but the big question that  everyone on the mac rumors podcast had  was why the boxing one on the right was  so much bigger than the one on the left  because they all thought it made sense  for the new rugged edition to be a  smaller apple watch se model at the low  end but in my opinion it's actually the  opposite i believe the new boxy design  is meant to be marketed as a pro model  that's going to be more expensive than  the regular series 8 because apple will  be able to bring the average sales price  up and offer the highest end features on  this new pro model first and if you  don't believe me i also have some  overwhelming evidence from the very  reliable display analyst ross young who  said that we should expect three  different apple watch display sizes in  2022 and that perfectly matches up to  more recent leaks that say that we are  in fact getting three new apple watches  this year a new se a regular series 8  and a new rugged edition but the most  important detail that ross young gave us  was that the third display size is  actually gonna be bigger than the  current series seven yes bigger which  would explain the larger size in john's  renders so in my opinion it makes sense  for the new apple watch se to have a  display size of 40 to 44 millimeters  just like the series 6 and then the new  regular series 8 model to have an  identical display from the series 7  which is 41 to 45 millimeters and then  the new rugged series 8 pro model to  come with a 42 to 46 millimeter display  size perfectly matching up to what ross  young leaked and this theory also  matches up to most of the other leaks  out there including john prosser's leaks  and it also matches up to simple common  sense because if you think about it the  best way to get people to pay more money  for an apple watch is to call it the pro  model just like they've done with  literally the rest of their products  like the iphone pro the mac pro and the  ipad pro and to go along with the pro  title they've got to give it a redesign  that looks nothing like every apple  watch that they've ever made before to  of course differentiate it and make it  look special so people will know when  someone paid extra for the pro model and  finally having a pro model would also  allow apple to throw in the most  expensive new technology on that model  first before slowly bringing it down to  the rest of the apple watch lineup just  like they've been doing with the ipad  pro and the iphone pro and the cool  thing about all of this is that apple  can guarantee that this new pro model  will be more rugged because of the flat  display glass that is going to be  stronger which is hidden behind the  metal rim  and they can offer it in titanium only  which will make it more tough but the  key point i want to make is that making  the display glass completely flat will  actually save apple a ton of internal  space which will allow them to throw in  a larger battery which is something that  people would definitely pay extra for  and it would make it worthy of the pro  title but going even further the new  larger flat design is literally the only  way that apple will be able to add mac  safe support to the apple watch just  like they did to both the airpods 3 and  the airpods pro case and if you don't  believe me mark german who is incredibly  reliable has been talking about apple  adding magsafe support to the apple  watch for months now and this new larger  pro model is the only way it makes sense  for this to happen so if you take a step  back and look at all these leaks  together i think this theory is by far  the most logical and it basically checks  all of the boxes in terms of the reports  from various different sources and with  that said i think it's very likely that  we'll be seeing this new boxy redesign  revealed at apple's september event just  seven months from now and if you totally  disagree with me go ahead and let me  know down in the comment section below  but if you enjoyed this video click that  circle above to subscribe for more  videos like this one thanks for watching  and we'll see you in the next one  [Music]
 

